#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# jacobi_p

#% text
# `jacobi_p(n, a, b, x)` gives the Jacobi polynomial P_n^(a, b)(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
jacobi_p(1, a, b, x)
#% output
#= x + (-1/2)*b + (1/2)*a + (1/2)*a*x + (1/2)*b*x

#% cell
jacobi_p(2, 1, 2, x)
#% output
#= -3/4 + (-3/2)*x + (21/4)*x^2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
jacobi_p(1.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= -0.016845432426635706

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gegenbauer_c`, `legendre_p`
